{“Background”: (“When Takeshi was 4 years old, his mother died in a traffic accident a few months after his younger sister Yumiko was born. Takeshi's father was deeply affected by the accident, causing him to go on a bender. It also affected his psyche, so he took out his frustrations and failures on his children, insulting and beating them. This continued until Takeshi turned 12 (and Yumiko 8), and they decided to work together to escape their distraught father. For months they wandered the civil war-torn streets penniless, signing up for any part-time job to get money for food, and going to sleep under a bridge, not sure if they would wake up the next day. This went on until the mafia stumbled upon them, as a result of which they hired Takeshi to clean up their dirty work, and a year and a half later to do the work himself in exchange for money and safety within the organization. Yumiko also wanted to help her older brother, but he refused, not wanting to put her in danger. After 4 years, the organization decided to get rid of Takeshi by giving him an impossible ultimatum and killing him after the deadline. But by the time he realized what was going on, it was too late: he was hunted down, knocked out, and had his limbs tied to the railroad tracks. When Takeshi woke up, he had only managed to free his legs before a freight train ran along the tracks, cutting off his hands. In the end, he barely made it to the nearest medical center on pure adrenaline and luck. He was given prosthetic hands, but they were of poor quality, so he and his sister had to have them rebuilt and modified. After six months, Takeshi was discharged from the hospital and was able to live a relatively normal life again, but the ghosts of his past still haunt him.”)}
